# Core project rules

Follow [RULES.md](RULES.md). Keep the MVP in [Overview.md](Overview.md).

- Yjs shared state for concurrent editing. Never last-write-wins HTTP document saves.
- Separate auth, persistence, collab transport, permissions, and editor UI.
- Authorize HTTP routes and WebSocket rooms. Room name access is not permission.
- Roles: `view`, `comment`, `edit`. Viewers cannot edit; commenters cannot edit content.
- Redis coordinates multiple collab instances; PostgreSQL/Prisma is the source of truth for users, pages, and roles.
- No canvas, billing, or enterprise admin in the MVP.
- Do not claim scale or convergence without recorded tests.
- Never commit secrets. Placeholders only in `.env.example`.
- Small focused changes. Update docs when contracts or setup change.
- Record decisions and open questions in `Memory.md`.
- Start every session by reading `Memory.md`. Before the first command and after every completed command/task, update its progress log. No secrets.
